rface-2:#1f1f21;--hp-code-kw:#8aa6c8;--hp-code-num:#b9b3a6}.homepage-preview-root .font-mono,.homepage-preview-root code,.homepage-preview-root pre{font-family:'Aeonik Mono',ui-monospace,monospace}</style><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Organization","name":"Prefect","url":"https://www.prefect.io","logo":"https://www.prefect.io/brand/prefect-logo-2026.png","description":"Orchestrate workflows with Prefect. Build AI applications with Horizon. Open-source foundations, production-ready platforms.","sameAs":["https://github.com/prefecthq","https://twitter.com/prefectio"]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"SoftwareApplication","name":"Prefect","applicationCategory":"DeveloperApplication","operatingSystem":"Cross-platform","description":"Prefect is an orchestration platform for running data pipelines and AI agents reliably in production, with durable execution, observability, and governance.","offers":{"@type":"Offer","price":"0","priceCurrency":"USD"},"aggregateRating":{"@type":"AggregateRating","ratingValue":4.5,"bestRating":5,"reviewCount":125}}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is Prefect?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Prefect is a workflow orchestration platform for data, ML, and agents. You write workflows as plain Python, and Prefect runs them durably in production: scheduling, retries, caching, and recovery are part of the platform rather than code you maintain. The open-source framework and Prefect Cloud share the same core engine."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can my coding agent write Prefect workflows?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. A Prefect workflow is ordinary Python with two decorators, so any coding agent that writes Python can produce a working flow, add retries, and deploy it without learning a DSL. Your engineers review and own the result, and the same is true for humans: if you can write a Python function, you can ship a Prefect flow."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How is Prefect different from Airflow?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Three differences do most of the work. Workflows are plain Python functions that can branch, loop, and create tasks at runtime, rather than DAGs declared up front. Durable execution is built into the engine, so retries, state, and crash recovery are not code you write. And with Prefect Cloud there is no scheduler for your team to host, upgrade, or page anyone about."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I have to run any infrastructure?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Only if you want to. Prefect Serverless runs flows on managed compute, so you can start with zero infrastructure. Teams with stricter requirements use the hybrid model instead: lightweight workers inside your environment run your code where your data already lives, while the control plane handles scheduling and visibility. That split is what clears most security reviews."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Prefect open source?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The Prefect framework is open source under the Apache 2.0 license, and it is the same engine Prefect Cloud runs. Cloud adds the managed control plane, enterprise authentication, and scale on top; it does not fork the framework."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does the Dagster Labs acquisition mean for Prefect?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Prefect acquired Dagster Labs in July 2026, bringing together two leading orchestration products. Nothing changes for users of either product: Dagster keeps its name and open-source license, and no action is required of any customer. The full announcement is at prefect.io/prefect-acquires-dagster."}}]}</script><div aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none fixed inset-0 z-50" style="opacity:0.04;mix-blend-mode:screen;background-image:url(/no
