=== retries.mdx ===
| ---
title: How to automatically rerun your workflow when it fails
sidebarTitle: Automatically rerun a workflow when it fails
keywords: ["retry", "failure", "error handling", "resilience", "automatic rerun"]
| ---

### Set the number of retries

To rerun your workflow when an exception is raised, set the `retries` parameter to an integer.

```python
from prefect import flow


@flow(retries=3)
def troublesome_workflow():
    raise Exception("oopsie daisy")
```

### Retry nested flows

When a parent flow retries a direct call to a [nested flow](/v3/concepts/flows#organize-flows-with-subflows-and-tasks),
Prefect reuses the child's completed result if it was [persisted](/v3/advanced/results).
Set `persist_result=True` on the child flow to enable result persistence.

If the child failed or completed without a persisted result, the parent retry creates a new child flow run.
The new run has its own retry budget, while the previous run keeps its state and history.
Because the child has a new flow-run ID, task caches that include the flow-run ID do not carry over from the previous child run.

### Wait between retries

To add a wait between retries, pass a value to the `retry_delay_seconds` parameter.

```python
from prefect import flow


@flow(retries=3, retry_delay_seconds=2.7182)
def troublesome_workflow():
    raise Exception("oopsie daisy")
=== retry-flow-runs.mdx ===
| ---
title: How to manually retry a flow run
sidebarTitle: Manually retry a flow run
keywords: ["retry", "flow run", "manual retry", "rerun", "failure recovery"]
| ---

Use `prefect flow-run retry` to re-execute a failed or cancelled flow run. The flow run keeps its original ID and parameters, but the `run_count` increments.

### Find flow runs to retry

List failed flow runs to find the name you need:

```bash
prefect flow-run ls --state FAILED
```

### Retry a deployment-based flow run

If the flow run was created from a deployment, retry schedules it for a worker to pick up:

```bash
prefect flow-run retry adventurous-crocodile
```

The flow run's state changes to `Scheduled` and a worker will pick it up for execution.

### Retry a local flow run

Flow runs created without a deployment require an `--entrypoint` to the flow code:

```bash
prefect flow-run retry adventurous-crocodile --entrypoint ./flows/my_flow.py:my_flow
```

The flow executes immediately in the current process.

### Retry by ID

If multiple flow runs share the same name, use the UUID instead:
